      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that passing an invalid class name as the `\"writers\"` config value causes `makeSpatialContext` to throw a `RuntimeException` with \"Unable to find format class\". Let me write an improved version with better naming, no unused imports, and clearer comments.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes the two unused imports (`JtsSpatialContextFactory`, `ShapeFactoryImpl`), renames the variable to `configWithInvalidWriterClass` for clarity, and adds a Javadoc comment and an inline comment explaining why the exception is thrown."
